3. Difference (-)
The difference of two sets contains elements that are in the first set but not in the second set.
A-B

contains the elements that are only in A and not in B.
Example:
X={aⓜ,bⓜ,cⓜ,dⓜ,e}
Y={aⓜ,cⓜ,fⓜ,g}

Therefore:
X-Y={dⓜ,e}
Y-X={fⓜ,g}

2.6 Complement of a Set
The complement of a set A, denoted as:
A^c

(or sometimes A^'), is the set of all elements in the universal set Uthat are NOT in A.
Example:
A={2ⓜ,4ⓜ,6}
U={2ⓜ,4ⓜ,6ⓜ,8ⓜ,10ⓜ,12}

Therefore:
A^c={8ⓜ,10ⓜ,12}

